      "math_academy_id": "e-843",
      "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac {6y + 2} {3xy + x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n    \\eqalign{\n        \\dfrac {6y + 2} {3xy + x} &= \\dfrac {6y + 2} {x(3y + 1)} \\[5pt] \n        &=\\dfrac {2(3y + 1)} {x(3y + 1)} \\[5pt] \n        &=\\dfrac {2\\cancel{(3y + 1)} } {x \\cancel{(3y + 1)} } \\[5pt] \n        &=\\dfrac {2 } {x}\n    }\n$$",
